  "body": "### Summary\nOperator decision Q-10 (2026-11-10): the moderator alert keeps the legacy mail fallback in release builds, **as the legacy app**. When a message has no alert link (for instance logged out), the app offers to write to the address the legacy app uses.\n\n### Facts\n- Legacy builds a `mailto:` to HFR's contact address, hard-coded, with the topic and message in the subject and body: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:4570-4584` @ `87fe0d1c` (the same address in `PlusTab.swift:150` and `Classes/PlusTableViewController.m:141`).\n- LOT-135 (#719, merged as 9cfec2f) reads the address from the build setting `MODERATOR_ALERT_MAIL_ADDRESS` → Info.plist `ModeratorAlertMailAddress`. It is empty by default, so there is no fallback today (spec `docs/lots/LOT-135-*.md`, Q-10).\n\n### Scope\n- Set the build setting to the legacy address in the shared, committed configuration (`App/Config/Shared.xcconfig`). This is not a secret: it is HFR's public contact address, already public in the legacy source. Write it once and cite the legacy line next to it.\n- Record the decision in the LOT-135 spec (Q-10 answered) and, if ADR 0007 is read as covering it, add one line saying a public contact address is not a key.\n- Keep the subject and body format of legacy (`MessagesView.swift:4570-4584`).\n- Test: a build with the setting offers the mail fallback for a message without an alert link; a build without it does not.\n\nM4. Origin: parity.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
